  "assessment": "The change replaces the hardcoded `st.DONE` / `st.FAILED` check with a call to `st.is_terminal()`. This correctly delegates status classification, ensuring that newly added terminal statuses like `CANCELLED` stop the SLA clock at their `ended_at` timestamp instead of defaulting to the current time. The change directly addresses the reported SLA inflation for self-cancelled jobs and aligns with the lifecycle specification.",
